# neo_hard: one hard non-aggressive SDE signature.
# 8-step tracked literal chain (AB CD EF GH IJ KL MN OP) separated by
# finite {1-3} byte gaps; OP is the terminal step. All literal words
# appear in scan.bin so the CP tier cannot discharge (no absent
# critical word) and the SDE tier runs. The chain never completes
# in-range (OP appears ONLY before the AB..MN runs) so SDE discharges.
# The many AB..MN occurrences keep a long carrying step-queue, which
# stresses the legacy two-pass SDE while neo's Q_m stays bounded.
# See README for the full design.
#
# cp_cover: coverage-only sig. Its single critical word uses all 16 hex
# nibbles so the AC-DFA alphabet is complete (hex_acdfa requires
# alpha_size==17). The word never appears in scan.bin, so the CP tier
# discharges it and it never reaches the SDE circuit.
cp_cover;Engine:51-255,Target:1;0;0123456789abcdef
sed_hard;Engine:51-255,Target:1;0;4142{1-3}4344{1-3}4546{1-3}4748{1-3}494a{1-3}4b4c{1-3}4d4e{1-3}4f50
